-- title:
--   Raynaud prolongation of the connected part into the Néron model
-- statement:
--   Fix $N_0$ non-zero and a prime $p$ with $p \nmid N_0$, a valuation subring $A$ of an algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$, level data $\Lambda$ at $(N_0,p,A)$ satisfying `IsJacobian`, a Néron object $O$ over $\Lambda$ and a Néron extension $F$ of $O$, with base $\operatorname{shBase} A$ attached to the valuation subring $\operatorname{shRing} A$ of the fixed field $\operatorname{invField} A$ of the inertia subgroup $A.\mathrm{inertiaSubgroupIn}\,\mathbb{Q}$. Assume: for every $m$ coprime to $p$, every inertia element $\sigma$ and every $x \in J_0(N_0p)[m]$ one has $\sigma\cdot x - x \in O.\mathrm{toricPts}\,m$ (the subgroup generated by the toric points); for every $m>0$ the same displacements lie in $O.\mathrm{finPts}\,m$ (generated by the $m$-torsion points whose section extends to the place); and $p \neq 2$. Let $V \le J_0(N_0p)[p]$ be an additive subgroup, $H_A$ a commutative cocommutative Hopf algebra over $\operatorname{shRing} A$, finite free of $p$-power rank, together with a bijection $e_A$ from $\operatorname{WithConv}$ of the $\operatorname{shRing} A$-algebra maps $H_A \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ onto $V$ sending convolution to addition and intertwining the action of $\operatorname{Aut}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\operatorname{invField} A)$ (if $g = \sigma \circ f$ pointwise then $e_A g = \sigma \cdot e_A f$), let $H_0$ be a local commutative cocommutative Hopf algebra over $\operatorname{shRing} A$, finite free of $p$-power rank, and $\pi : H_A \to H_0$ a bialgebra homomorphism. Then there is a morphism $u : \operatorname{Spec} H_0 \to F.\mathrm{Nfull}$ such that: $u$ followed by $F.\mathrm{gN}$ is the morphism induced by $\operatorname{shRing} A \to H_0$; for every commutative $\operatorname{shRing} A$-algebra $C$, all $\varphi, \psi : H_0 \to C$ and all sections $x,y$ of $F.\mathrm{gN}$ over $\operatorname{Spec} C$ with underlying morphisms $\operatorname{Spec}\varphi$ followed by $u$, resp. $\operatorname{Spec}\psi$ followed by $u$, the product $F.\mathrm{LN}.\mathrm{mul}$ of $x$ and $y$ has underlying morphism $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the convolution $\varphi * \psi$ followed by $u$; and for every $f_0 : H_0 \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, $\operatorname{Spec} f_0$ followed by $u$ is the underlying morphism of $F.\mathrm{ptsN}$ at the point $e_A(f_0 \circ \pi) \in V \le J_0(N_0p)$.
--
--   This is the prolongation step, after Raynaud, in Ribet's level-lowering argument: the connected part $\operatorname{Spec} H_0$ of a finite flat $p$-group scheme realising $V \le J_0(N_0p)[p]$ maps into the Néron model over the inertia-invariant base, multiplicatively for the relative group law and compatibly with the prescribed $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points. It is used in the passage from Hopf-algebra data to finiteness statements for $F.\mathrm{ptsN}$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_JZeroNeronObjectAtP_NeronExtension_exists_forall_mul_eq_specMap_forall_specMap_comp_eq_ptsN_of_bialgHom_of_isLocalRing.lean

